Requirements: 47   with obligations: 46   deliberately none: 1   unaccounted for: 0

[task-01] `decompose` returns a flat list of obligations plus a flat list of open
    questions. A response covering 20 of a task file's 29 requirements is exactly as
    well-formed as one covering all 29, so nothing downstream can notice that nine
    requirements produced nothing. Gate 1 for #195 lost 4 of 15 Completion expectations
    and 5 of 8 Scope exclusions this way, and the review reported no gap.
    -> obligation-requirement-to-obligation-mapping  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-02, completion-02)
       Return decomposition results as a mapping from each requirement to its obligation
       disposition, so requirement-level outcomes are recorded explicitly.
    -> obligation-record-none-disposition  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-02, completion-02, completion-03)
       Represent requirements that yield no obligation as recorded mapping entries with
       their reason.
    -> obligation-regression-suite-195-results-unchanged  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-12)
       Preserve the pass/fail results of regression suite #195.

[task-02] Make decomposition return a mapping from requirement to obligation, so that a
    requirement producing nothing is a recorded fact rather than an absence.
    -> obligation-requirement-to-obligation-mapping  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, completion-02)
       Return decomposition results as a mapping from each requirement to its obligation
       disposition, so requirement-level outcomes are recorded explicitly.
    -> obligation-record-none-disposition  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, completion-02, completion-03)
       Represent requirements that yield no obligation as recorded mapping entries with
       their reason.

[task-03] Separately, and independent of that defect: a reader auditing a breakdown
    cannot see which requirement each obligation came from. `Obligation.source_spans`
    points at a character offset, so the trace runs one way and only to text, never to
    an identified requirement.
    -> obligation-obligation-source-requirement-trace  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Provide traceability from each obligation back to the requirement it came from,
       not only to character offsets.

[task-04] This change is representational. It alters the shape of what decomposition
    returns, not the obligations it derives.
    -> obligation-representational-change-only  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the set of obligations derived from a task file while changing only the
       representation returned by decomposition.

[constraint-01] A requirement registry is derived from
    `requirement/task_file.py::parse_task_file`.
    -> obligation-requirement-registry-from-parser  [functional/explicit]
       Derive the requirement registry from `requirement/task_file.py::parse_task_file`.

[constraint-02] Requirement ids are assigned by the code, never by the model.
    -> obligation-requirement-ids-assigned-by-code  [invariant/explicit]
       Assign requirement ids in code rather than by the model.

[constraint-03] A requirement id is its section and its ordinal within that section, in
    parse order.
    -> obligation-requirement-id-section-ordinal  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-07)
       Form each requirement id from its section and its ordinal within that section, in
       parse order.

[constraint-04] Each registry entry carries the `TextSpan` of the requirement it
    identifies.
    -> obligation-requirement-registry-textspan  [functional/explicit]
       Attach the `TextSpan` of the identified requirement to each registry entry.

[constraint-05] The requirement-to-obligation relation is many-to-many.
    -> obligation-many-to-many-relation  [invariant/explicit]
       Model the requirement-to-obligation relation as many-to-many.

[constraint-06] An obligation serving two requirements is linked to both.
    -> obligation-obligation-linked-to-both-requirements  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-05)
       Link an obligation that serves two requirements to both requirements.

[constraint-07] An obligation is never duplicated so that each requirement can hold its
    own copy.
    -> obligation-no-obligation-duplication  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves completion-06)
       Keep each obligation as a single object rather than duplicating it per
       requirement.

[constraint-08] Every requirement carries exactly one disposition.
    -> obligation-one-disposition-per-requirement  [invariant/explicit]
       Assign exactly one disposition to every requirement.

[constraint-09] The dispositions are: yielded obligations; deliberately yields none,
    with a reason; raised an open question instead.
    -> obligation-disposition-kinds  [functional/explicit]
       Support the three disposition kinds: yielded obligations, deliberately yields
       none with a reason, and raised an open question instead.

[constraint-10] The mapping is persisted in the structured review state that
    `review_state.py` and `review_store.py` already define.
    -> obligation-persist-mapping-in-review-state  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-10)
       Persist the requirement-to-obligation mapping in the structured review state
       defined by `review_state.py` and `review_store.py`.

[constraint-11] The mapping is rendered in the §16 report.
    -> obligation-render-mapping-in-section-16-report  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-04)
       Render the requirement-to-obligation mapping in the §16 report.

[constraint-12] `requirement/obligations.py::_user_prompt` passes typed, identified
    fields.
    -> obligation-user-prompt-typed-identified-fields  [functional/explicit]
       Have `_user_prompt` pass typed, identified fields.

[constraint-13] `_user_prompt` does not pass `parsed.source`.
    -> obligation-user-prompt-omits-parsed-source  [invariant/explicit]
       Keep `_user_prompt` from passing `parsed.source`.

[constraint-14] The decomposer receives no `ChangeSet`.
